# {{.project_name}}

Standalone evaluation project generated from the AAI platform template
(`evaluation-project`): curated datasets, reusable scorers, pinned
baselines, a two-tier CI gate, and published results.

## Local setup

```bash
az login
export DATABRICKS_HOST={{.workspace_host}}
export DATABRICKS_AUTH_TYPE=azure-cli
python scripts/install_core.py
python -m pip install -r requirements.lock
python -m pip install -e '.[dev]'
pytest -q
python evals/offline_checks.py   # tier 1 — deterministic, zero credentials
```

## How this project evaluates

- **Datasets** — `evals/data/golden_cases.json` is the reviewed regression
  suite (gates releases; grow it toward 150+ cases and convert every
  production failure into a case). `edge_cases.json` is the capability suite
  (deliberately hard; report-only). `answer_sheet.json` holds recorded
  answers so scoring works without calling the application.
  `scripts/sync_dataset.py` publishes cases to the governed UC dataset
  `{{.catalog}}.{{.schema}}.{{.dataset_name}}`.
- **Scorers** — `src/app/scorers.py` holds deterministic code scorers (pure
  functions, unit-tested, run in both tiers). `src/app/judges.py` routes the
  Correctness/Safety judges through the gateway-fronted `judge-model`
  endpoint; align judges against human labels first
  (`notebooks/01_align_judge.py`).
- **Gate** — thresholds live in `evals/gate_config.json`. Tier 1
  (`evals/offline_checks.py`, PR CI) applies the code-scorer thresholds to
  the answer sheet. Tier 2 (`evals/evaluate.py`, credentialed) runs code
  scorers + judges, enforces every threshold plus regression against
  `evals/baseline.json`, and publishes a markdown report to the CI step
  summary. After a released run passes: `--update-baseline`.
- **Targets** — score recorded answers (default) or a live endpoint:
  `python evals/evaluate.py --mode endpoint` (configure `target-model` in
  `aai-platform.yml`).

Deploy the scheduled suite with `databricks bundle validate -t dev` and
`databricks bundle deploy -t dev` (uncomment the cron block in
`resources/evaluation_job.yml` for continuous evaluation).

The platform team must onboard this repository (main-branch federated
credential, service principal, constrained compute, non-secret repository
variables) before the deploy workflow is enabled.
